 AudioStreamEffectApplicator)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3156686613/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3333324161","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107523#issuecomment-3333324161","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107523","id":3333324161,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Grn2B","user":{"login":"RoyBerardo","id":32561682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTYxNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32561682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo","html_url":"https://github.com/RoyBerardo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-25T10:33:03Z","updated_at":"2025-09-25T10:33:33Z","body":"Forgot to comment - Changed it to `AudioStreamWithEffects`, seems that's the most popular one. Thank you KoBeWi for the suggestion!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3333324161/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3381083677","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107523#issuecomment-3381083677","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107523","id":3381083677,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Jhz4d","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-08T11:28:35Z","updated_at":"2025-10-08T11:28:35Z","body":"I tested and it works correctly, though I found it weird that each effect has a bypass flag and process when bypassed; like, if you want to bypass effect, why de-bypass it? Though then I've read the description (both in the PR and in the documentation), and I can't tell difference when this flag is enabled.\r\n\r\nAlso I wonder if it's possible to get AudioEffectInstance from the effects? Currently instances can only be retrieved with `get_bus_effect_instance()` from AudioServer, but it only works with buses.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3381083677/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3396772333","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107523#issuecomment-3396772333","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107523","id":3396772333,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KdqHt","user":{"login":"RoyBerardo","id":32561682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTYxNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32561682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo","html_url":"https://github.com/RoyBerardo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-13T10:10:16Z","updated_at":"2025-11-06T10:46:00Z","body":"> I tested and it works correctly, though I found it weird that each effect has a bypass flag and process when bypassed; like, if you want to bypass effect, why de-bypass it? Though then I've read the description (both in the PR and in the documentation), and I can't tell difference when this flag is enabled.\r\n\r\nWhen it comes to effects like reverb, if you bypass it while audio is playing, it sort of \"stores\" the reverb state and holds onto that until you un-bypass. This means that when you un-bypass reverb, it will emit the reverb that it was \"storing\" when the reverb was bypassed. If the stored reverb is released during silence, that can be quite jarring. Processing the reverb while bypassed means that you won't hear the effect but it will still be running under the hood in order to prevent a burst of sound.\r\n\r\nThis all being said, your comment is making me think that perhaps this should be something to tackle from the side of the effect, not the side of whatever processes the effects. From what I've seen, effects really have no way of knowing if they're bypassed or not, so they cannot do actions when bypassed/un-bypassed, such as resetting their state in the case of reverb. May be good to open an issue/proposal about this. There would be no need for \"process when bypassed\" if effects could do this. Plus, this issue isn't exclusive to `AudioStreamWithEffects`, it happens with effects placed on busses as well.\r\n\r\n> Also I wonder if it's possible to get AudioEffectInstance from the effects? Currently instances can only be retrieved with `get_bus_effect_instance()` from AudioServer, but it only works with buses.\r\n\r\nOh actually I completely forgot to do this. I'll add that.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3396772333/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3536461828","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107523#issuecomment-3536461828","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107523","id":3536461828,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SyiAE","user":{"login":"RoyBerardo","id":32561682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTYxNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32561682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo","html_url":"https://github.com/RoyBerardo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-15T12:52:13Z","updated_at":"2025-11-15T12:52:13Z","body":"Updated with the above suggestions, plus a couple more things.\r\n\r\nChanges:\r\n- Removed the editor plugin (Switched from ADD_ARRAY to ADD_ARRAY_COUNT)\r\n- Made `effect_playback->effect_instances` a LocalVector\r\n- Added `AudioServer` locking/unlocking to avoid thread issues\r\n- All functions that use indexes can now use negative indexes\r\n- Removed \"Process when bypassed\"\r\n- Added `AudioStreamPlaybackWithEffects.get_effect_instance()` and `AudioStreamPlaybackWithEffects. get_effect_instance_count()` (Originally added the second function for testing/debugging, but figured it wouldn't hurt to keep it around)\r\n- Added documentation for `AudioStreamPlaybackWithEffects`\r\n- Looooots of documentation changes\r\n\r\nAppreciate all the review and feedback!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3536461828/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4300451427","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107523#issuecomment-4300451427","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107523","id":4300451427,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAFOuYw","user":{"login":"Akosmo","id":95504962,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbFKQg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95504962?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo","html_url":"https://github.com/Akosmo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akosmo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-22T22:56:10Z","updated_at":"2026-04-22T22:56:10Z","body":"Adding here something we discussed in the last audio meeting:\r\nHaving this added to the engine allow us to remove the high shelf filter embedded in `_mix_step_for_channel()` in the AudioServer, which isn't the perfect approach for `AudioStreamPlayer3D`'s attenuation.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4300451427/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4633092628","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107523#issuecomment-4633092628","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107523","id":4633092628,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFCdiFA","user":{"login":"RoyBerardo","id":32561682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTYxNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32561682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo","html_url":"https://github.com/RoyBerardo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerardo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-05T15:29:27Z","updated_at":"2026-06-05T15:29:27Z","body":"Exciting to see that we can add descriptions to array properties now! Just added those two descriptions, would appreciate some eyes on those from someone who is better at docs than I am. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4633092628/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4947901603","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107523#issuecomment-4947901603","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107523","id":4947901603,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJur8ow","user":{"login":"goatchurchprime","id":677254,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NzI1NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/677254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime","html_url":"https://github.com/goatchurchprime","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-11T16:57:20Z","updated_at":"2026-07-11T16:59:51Z","body":"I've hit a snag while trying to replicate the capabilities of the AudioStreamPlayer3D that are internal to the AudioServer using this feature.  \r\n\r\nIn order to programatically make sine waves as input I need access to the AudioStreamGeneratorPlayback for the stream that is playing so I can push in the frames.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"642\" height=\"341\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2cce39d9-7883-401d-a422-023752453f94\" />\r\n\r\nIs there any way to get to this, or is this a flaw in the use of the `AudioStreamGeneratorPlayback` object that it is only ever accessible when it is the top level stream in the AudioStreamPlayer?\r\n https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_audiostreamgeneratorplayback.html","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4947901603/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4961116101","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107523#issuecomment-4961116101","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107523","id":4961116101,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJ7SfxQ","user":{"login":"goatchurchprime","id":677254,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NzI1NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/677254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime","html_url":"https://github.com/goatchurchprime","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-13T18:10:20Z","updated_at":"2026-07-13T18:10:20Z","body":"After some use of this feature [in a project](https://github.com/goatchurchprime/AudioStreamEffects3D/tree/useaudiostreamwitheffects) to replicate and expose the hidden AudioEffects which implement the `AudioStreamPlayer3D`, I'm not as positive about this feature as I had been earlier. \r\n\r\nThe problem is that when you wrap the `AudioStream` of an `AudioStreamPlayer` into this new `AudioStreamWithEffects`:\r\n * you lose access to the `AudioStreamPlayback` of the inner `AudioStream` (so you can't use `AudioStreamGenerator`), \r\n *  you lose the polyphony feature where you can call `AudioStreamPlayer.play()` multiple times and the `AudioServer` spawns new simultaneously playing `AudioStreamPlaybacks` up to the quantity of `max_polyphony`.\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, this feature doesn't appear to give us any new features that can't already be implemented by inserting a new unique bus whenever we want to assign effects onto a single AudioStreamPlayer.(*)\r\n\r\n(*) Not quite accurate, since it allows for the application of effects before the spatial attenuation applied by AudioStreamPlayer3D.  However, once the AudioStreamPlayer3D's audioeffects are exposed on a bus, you would have the ability to insert further effects in front or behind this spatialization effect.  This is mostly not a big deal since the majority of effects commute (makes no difference the order they apply), but some do not.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4961116101/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]